From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:04:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/161] drm/xe/vm: use kvmalloc for the VMA ops page-table
 update array

On resume the rebind worker queues one page-table update op per VMA.
A big game has tens of thousands of VMAs, so the array outgrows what
kmalloc can hand out (4 MiB with 384-byte ops at about 10,900 VMAs),
the allocation fails and the next execbuf returns -ENOMEM: games like
Final Fantasy VII Rebirth report "out of memory" right after a resume.

The array is only touched by the CPU, so fall back to vmalloc when
kmalloc can't satisfy it. Same change as drm-xe-next "drm/xe: Use
kvmalloc for the VMA ops page-table update array" (SteamOS #2962).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
index 67819deb45..f646a4aa07 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/xe/xe_vm.c
@@ -662,9 +662,9 @@ static int xe_vma_ops_alloc(struct xe_vma_ops *vops, bool array_of_binds)
 			continue;
 
 		vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops =
-			kmalloc_objs(*vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops,
-				     vops->pt_update_ops[i].num_ops,
-				     GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL | __GFP_NOWARN);
+			kvmalloc_objs(*vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops,
+				      vops->pt_update_ops[i].num_ops,
+				      GFP_KERNEL | __GFP_RETRY_MAYFAIL | __GFP_NOWARN);
 		if (!vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops)
 			return array_of_binds ? -ENOBUFS : -ENOMEM;
 	}
@@ -701,7 +701,7 @@ static void xe_vma_ops_fini(struct xe_vma_ops *vops)
 	xe_vma_svm_prefetch_ops_fini(vops);
 
 	for (i = 0; i < XE_MAX_TILES_PER_DEVICE; ++i)
-		kfree(vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops);
+		kvfree(vops->pt_update_ops[i].ops);
 }
 
 static void xe_vma_ops_incr_pt_update_ops(struct xe_vma_ops *vops, u8 tile_mask, int inc_val)
